hey this is pressure Locker many people  have been confused by this problem on  Facebook and Twitter in this video I'm  going to present two different ways to  arrive at the correct answer one way to  solve this problem is to translate the  numerical equation into a sentence  imagine all the quantities involve money  the equation starts out with 7 which  will translate as meaning that you start  out with $7 the equation then has plus 7  divided by 7 this is interpreted as  receiving a 1/7 chair of $7 a 1/7 chair  of $7 is $1 and you're receiving the  money so you're going to want to add $1  we then have plus 7 times 7 that can be  interpreted as receiving 7 dollars a  total of 7 different times  how much money do you get 7 times 7 is  equal to 49 so that means you receive 49  more dollars finally we have minus 7  which means that seven dollars is taken  away from you we subtract seven dollars  how much money do you end up with at the  end 7 plus 1 is 8 8 plus 49 is 57 minus  7 is 50 you would end up with $50 and  the correct answer to this equation is  50 this problem is also a good reminder  about the order of operations this is a  hierarchy in which operations are  evaluated we have parentheses brackets  exponents orders multiplication division  and then finally addition subtraction  these can be remembered by PEMDAS or  botanist if you have operations of the  same precedence you want to evaluate  them from left to right we don't have  any parentheses or exponents but we do  have a multiplication and a division so  we want to evaluate these before we  evaluate the additions or the  subtractions we have a division of 7  divided by 7 and we have a mole  duplication of seven times seven 7/7  evaluates to 1 and seven times seven  evaluates to 49 we substitute these  results into our equation we have 7 plus  1 plus 49 minus 7 we now only have  addition and subtraction which we can  evaluate from left to right 7 plus 1 is  equal to 8 8 plus 49 is equal to 57 57  minus 7 is equal to 50 and that gets us  our correct result of 50 did you figure  this out thanks for watching this video  please subscribe to my channel I make  videos on math and game theory you can  catch from a blog mind your decisions  which you can follow on Facebook Google+  and patreon you can catch me on social  media at pressure Locker and if you  liked this video please check out my  books there links in the video  description
 

